│▸ t2  elevated    4 dreams · 3 sets   │ ◆SpeculativeLabel                                         │
│  t1  covered     3 dreams · 3 sets   │                                                           │
│  t3  recurring   2 dreams · 1 set    │ t2 · A map of the labyrinth                               │
│  t0  superseded by t2                │ elevated: proposed through the dream source               │
│                                      │ in 4 dreams, 3 distinct seed sets                         │
│                                      │                                                           │
│                                      │ (the theme's summary)                                     │
│                                      │ ideas: 2026-10-12.i4, 2026-10-15.i9, …                    │
│                                      │ How often an idea came back says nothing                  │
│                                      │ about whether it's right.                                 │
│                                      ├───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│                                      │ ? explain                                                 │
├──────────────────────────────────────┴───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ ◆KeyBar                                                                                          │
└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
note: from the dream review's theme registry. Distinct seed sets matter
because unchanged project state gives the same seeds: a theme counts as
recurring only when it came back from different material.

@due
┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ Dream                                                                     speculative · esc back │
├──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ Dreams · Picks · Themes · [Due]                                                                  │
├──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ A dream is due: a reflection ran since the last dream. Run /dream in the Claude pane.            │
│ Waiting: the dream from 2026-10-15-2 has picks not synced yet.                                   │
│ Dream review: not due (2 of 4 dreams since the last review).                                     │
│                                                                                                  │
│ Experiment                                                                                       │
│ Dreams: 6 · picks: 22 · synced 9 · applied 5 · built 2                                           │
│ Totals across every dream. The experiment's breakdown is `daedalus dream log`.                   │
│                                                                                                  │
│ s ask Claude to run /dream · ? explain                                                           │
├──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ ◆KeyBar                                                                                          │
└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
note: computed when shown (`dream due` without writing due.json). The
experiment lines are totals across every dream, never split by mode: a
per-mode count would move with one mode as picks are applied or built, and
next to the Dreams and Picks tabs that would tell a reader which mode made a
dream. The per-mode breakdown stays in `daedalus dream log`.

@off
┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ Dream                                                                     speculative · esc back │
├──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ Dreaming is off.                                                                                 │
│                                                                                                  │
│ A dream is a protected phase where Daedalus generates widely about where this project            │
│ could go: seeds from what it already keeps, the dream, then a cold waking pass that picks        │
│ three to five ideas. You judge them afterwards; picks reach the roadmap only as proposals        │
│ you apply or drop. A dream is never evidence.                                                    │
│                                                                                                  │
│ Turn it on:  daedalus config dream.enabled true   (add --project for this project only)          │
│ Then a dream is due after each reflection run, or ask for one with /dream [theme].               │
│                                                                                                  │
│ s ask Claude about dreaming · ? explain                                                          │
├──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ ◆KeyBar                                                                                          │
└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
note: dream.enabled unset means off. The screen teaches instead of showing
nothing.

## ◆SpeculativeLabel

@label
┌───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ ◇ speculative: a dream, not a proposal, not evidence, not │
│   reviewed. Nothing in Daedalus reads it as fact.         │
└───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
note: above every dream text on Dreams, Picks and Themes. A text tag, not a
colour, so it survives any theme.
